                <pb facs="0828" n="730" sameAs="frus:frus1920v01/pg730"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.48g/81: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Crane</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Acting Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-01-05T16:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 5,
                                1921—4 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received January 5—10
                    a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>4. Your 400, December 29, 3 p.m. Conditions of all Legations must be met before
                    surtax can be levied. Entire matter still under consideration. Date [of]
                    beginning of tax not yet certain.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Crane</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
